Practical Prep

During experiment, measure Air Temperature (K) with thermometer. Obtain Barometric Pressure (Pa) from the KNMI website for Rotterdam the Hague airport.

Connect aerofoil pressure holes to manometer.

Connect tappings 1,3,5,7,9, 11 (lower surface) to the FIRST set of manometer tubes.
Tappings 2,4,6,8,10,12 (upper surface) connect to the NEXT set of tubes.
The 13th tube is left OPEN so all pressures are with respect to atmospheric pressure.

The 14th (and last) tube is used to measure the pressure in the airbox, and at the inlet. So it needs to be swapped.

Per AoA do the following:
- Measure ambient pressure and air temperature
- Connect the 14th manometer opening to the airbox and measure the pressure p_t
- Connect the 14th manometer opening to the static pressure tapping in the inlet and measure this pressure, p_inf
- Measure all pressures from the aerofoil tappings.

